ructions", "contents": [{"content": " Talk about what you wish you could change about yourself.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter and Online Dating", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Finding Your Other Half", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking about Wishes and Imaginary Situations  ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">\u201cI wish ... \u201d</span> to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The verb <span class=\"italic\">wish</span> introduces an idea. After <span class=\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense. <br/><br/> I wish I knew ... <br/> I wish I had ... <br/> I wish you were ... <br/> I wish I was/were ... <br/><br/>  Structure: <br/> Wish + Simple Past tense", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish I were as successful with girls as you are. <br/><br/> I wish I was less awkward.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" I want to be as successful as you, but I'm not.<br/><br/>  I want to be less awkward but I can't.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I wish she liked me.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She probably doesn't like me.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "It is possible to use either <span class=\"strong\">was</span> or <span class=\"strong\">were</span> in the structure.  <span class=\"strong\">Were</span> is the more grammatically correct way to form the sentence, but <span class=\"strong\">was</span> is common in conversation. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modal Verbs for Speculating", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "  You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> may</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>  Must = It's very likely. <br> Must not/Could not/Can't = It's not possible.<br> May/Might/Can/Could = It's possible.<br/> May not/Might not = It's possible this is not true.<br> <br> You can use them in the present or perfect tenses. When you use them in the perfect tense, you are speculating about the past. <br> For example:  <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">may have been</span> busy when you tried to call. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That must feel natural for you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's very likely it's natural for you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> It can't be hard for you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's not possible that it's hard for you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I could've fallen for her.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible I would have fallen for her.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That may not have been easy for you.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible it wasn't easy for you.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "*Remember that in conversation, using the contracted form of the verb phrase is common (could have = could've).", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to match up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work well together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The date was great. I thought we matched up pretty well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation about dating.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lead on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to let someone believe things that may not be true", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I realized that she was leading me on, so we broke up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hit it off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get along well immediately", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We hit it off immediately and had a lot of fun on our first date.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fall for ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to have strong romantic feelings towards somebody", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I could have fallen for her, but I realized that she was leading me on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "head over heels", "type": "name"}, {"content": "madly in love", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I fell head over heels for a girl who was into comics.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have good chemistry", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to share many things in common with someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you have good chemistry with someone, you'll know straightaway.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le11ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of 8-10 things you wish you could change about yourself. They could be related to physical appearance, personality or emotions. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of them, and give one or two reasons why you would like to change them. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Say how different you would be if these things could change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to your partner's list. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about wishes and imaginary situations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss friendships and relationships.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give opinions and I speculate about feelings and reactions.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}